  "description": "FAWLIA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H120 Gd4 N8 Ni8 O38 4+,4(Cl1 O4 1-),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1B (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2B (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3B (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4B (Ni) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.065-3.997 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 83.07-115.44°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4Ni8(OH)8(L)8(O2CR)8(MeOH)6](ClO4)4·4H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Gd(III), Ni(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
